es-rgds-launchonce: one game launch at a time; a launch request made while a game ran is dropped

A launch only schedules the game (a transition, or for the rnds theme a 1 ms animation) and returns. A second
ViewController::launch() before that animation finished replaced it, which ran the first game at once, and the second
one started after it: two launch requests 0.15 s apart started the game twice (an RG DS Plus, 2026-10-05). Now a launch
is ignored while another is starting or running (GuiComponent::isLaunchTransitionRunning), with a warning in ES's log,
for 10 s at most: a view change can cancel the launch's animation and its callback (cancelAnimation), which would
leave the flag set and every later launch ignored.

The HTTP API's /launch is queued on the UI thread, which waits while a game runs: a request that came in meanwhile ran
after the game, as a second start nobody asked for at that moment. It is dropped now when it was received before the
last game handed back (ViewController::lastGameEndedAt). Both times come from a steady clock (ViewController::monoMs):
SDL_GetTicks starts again when ES re-initialises SDL around a game it closes its window for (every launch but DraStic's
fast switch), which let a request made during such a game through as a second start (seen in a test with two /launch
requests 0.15 s apart).

diff --git a/es-app/src/services/HttpServerThread.cpp b/es-app/src/services/HttpServerThread.cpp
index ab8f9306..e1042df0 100644
--- a/es-app/src/services/HttpServerThread.cpp
+++ b/es-app/src/services/HttpServerThread.cpp
@@ -620,7 +620,16 @@ void HttpServerThread::run()
 				if (file->getFullPath() == path || file->getPath() == path)
 				{
 					Window* w = mWindow;
-					mWindow->postToUiThread([w, file]() {
+					long long receivedAt = ViewController::monoMs();
+					mWindow->postToUiThread([w, file, receivedAt]() {
+						// ROCKNIXDS: the UI thread waits for a running game; a request that came meanwhile is not
+						// for the menu that comes back (es-rgds-launchonce)
+						long long ended = ViewController::lastGameEndedAt();
+						if (ended != 0 && receivedAt < ended)
+						{
+							LOG(LogWarning) << "Launch request for " << file->getPath() << " ignored: it came while a game was running";
+							return;
+						}
 						w->cancelScreenSaver();
 						ViewController::get()->launch(file);
 					});
